`),sampleAnswer:["## Process: Esterification — synthesis of methyl ethanoate","","**Chemical equation:**","$$\\mathrm{CH_3OH + CH_3COOH \\underset{\\Delta}{\\xrightarrow{\\text{conc. }H_2SO_4}} CH_3COOCH_3 + H_2O}$$","","**Selection of reagents:**","Methanol and ethanoic acid are both relatively low-toxicity reagents that are readily available in school laboratories.","Concentrated sulfuric acid is used as an acid catalyst (and dehydrating agent) to speed up the reaction.","These reagents were chosen because they are accessible and their reaction produces a well-known ester.","","**Reaction conditions:**","The reaction is performed under **reflux**: the mixture is heated gently in a round-bottomed flask fitted with a condenser.","Reflux allows heating to increase the rate of reaction without losing volatile reagents or products,","and avoids pressure build-up that would occur in a sealed vessel.","The reaction is allowed to proceed for approximately 30–60 minutes.","","**Hazards and safety precautions:**","- Methanol and ethanoic acid are **flammable** — use a heating mantle or hot water bath instead of a Bunsen burner; keep away from open flames.","- Concentrated sulfuric acid is **highly corrosive** — use small quantities; wear safety glasses and gloves; add acid to the reaction mixture carefully.","- Ethanoic acid vapour is **irritating** — perform the experiment in a fume cupboard or well-ventilated area.","","**Yield and purity:**","Esterification is a **reversible equilibrium** reaction, so the yield of methyl ethanoate is limited (typically 50–65% under simple conditions).","Yield can be improved by using excess of one reagent or removing water (the by-product) during the reaction.","The raw product contains unreacted alcohol, acid, water and catalyst.","To purify, the product mixture is washed with sodium carbonate solution (to neutralise acid and remove it), then with water, and finally dried over anhydrous $\\mathrm{Na_2SO_4}$ before distillation to collect pure methyl ethanoate (bp $57\\ \\mathrm{^\\circ C}$)."].join(`
