`),marks:2},{question:"Explain how the Reserve Bank of Australia (RBA) maintains the cash rate target.",sampleAnswer:["The RBA uses a policy interest rate corridor and its Exchange Settlement Account system to keep the market cash rate close to the target.","Because banks can borrow from the RBA at a rate above the target and deposit funds at a rate below the target, inter-bank rates tend to move toward the target rate.","The RBA can also use domestic market operations and reserve management to support that target."].join(`
