`),choices:e,sampleAnswer:{correctChoiceIndex:2,explanation:["A rendered sketch is the most appropriate method for communicating initial design ideas.","","At the initial stage of a design project, ideas are still exploratory and subject to change.","A rendered sketch quickly and clearly conveys the designer's visual concept to the client","in an accessible way, enabling early feedback before significant time or resources are committed.","","A prototype is too costly and time-consuming to produce at the initial stage.","A written report does not effectively communicate visual and spatial ideas.","A technical diagram is detailed and precise, but more appropriate for the later stages","of the design process, not initial concept communication."].join(`
