`)}}}},ntt={id:"design_and_technology/2025/q02",version:1,variants:1,generate(t){return{question:"Which of the following should a designer prioritise when designing a product for children?",choices:["Using the most affordable materials available","Selecting materials with high aesthetic appeal","Ensuring that materials are safe, durable and non-toxic","Creating a complex user interface for extended engagement and durability"],sampleAnswer:{correctChoiceIndex:2,explanation:["When designing for children, safety is the primary responsibility.","","Children may put objects in their mouths, handle products roughly,","or be exposed to materials for extended periods. A designer must ensure","materials are safe (no sharp edges or choking hazards), durable (able to","withstand rough use), and non-toxic (no harmful chemicals).","","Affordability, aesthetics and complex interfaces are secondary considerations","compared to the fundamental duty of care for a vulnerable user group."].join(`
