`)}}}},ott={id:"design_and_technology/2025/q04",version:1,variants:1,generate(t){return{question:"Why is it necessary to experiment and test for durability?",choices:["To check the market demand for the product","To reduce the environmental impact of the product","To determine if the product can be sold at a lower price","To understand how the product functions under different conditions"],sampleAnswer:{correctChoiceIndex:3,explanation:["Testing for durability is necessary to understand how a product performs","and functions under different conditions — such as repeated use, physical stress,","extreme temperatures, or exposure to moisture.","","This testing ensures the product meets performance standards and can withstand","real-world use without failing prematurely.","","Market demand, environmental impact, and pricing are separate considerations","not directly addressed by durability testing."].join(`
`)}}}},att={id:"design_and_technology/2025/q05",version:1,variants:1,generate(t){return{question:["Which of the following is the main purpose of analysing data collected","when designing a project?"].join(" "),choices:["To organise information into tables and charts","To ensure the data looks visually appealing to investors","To draw meaningful conclusions that guide decision-making","To collect as much data as possible about manufacturing trends"],sampleAnswer:{correctChoiceIndex:2,explanation:["The main purpose of analysing data in a design project is to draw meaningful","conclusions that guide decision-making.","","Data analysis transforms raw information into actionable insights, helping","designers make informed choices about materials, user needs, functionality,","and design direction.","","Organising data into tables and charts is a method used during analysis,","not the purpose. Visual appeal and collecting more data are not the goals","of data analysis."].join(`
`)}}}},rtt={id:"design_and_technology/2025/q06",version:1,variants:1,generate(t){return{question:["Collaboration with other designers can improve the outcomes of a design project by"].join(""),choices:["reducing the need for communication and feedback.","ensuring the design project is managed by an expert.","increasing the manufacturing cost of the design project.","utilising design experience for different aspects of the project."],sampleAnswer:{correctChoiceIndex:3,explanation:["Collaboration improves design outcomes by combining the different knowledge,","skills and experience of multiple designers across various aspects of the project.","","For example, one designer may specialise in ergonomics while another excels","in materials selection — their combined expertise produces a better outcome","than working alone.","","Collaboration increases the need for communication (not reduces it),","does not guarantee expert management, and does not necessarily increase","manufacturing costs."].join(`
